; BREAKER FINDING — RUST-TARGET DIFFERENTIAL: calling an exported entry whose parameter is a STRING with a
; string argument fails to build on the rust target (E0308 in the generated driver), while wasm cleanly
; DECLINES. An exported `(def (main (: s String)) …)` invoked via `(call main (: "abc" String))`:
;   wasm: DECLINES ("compiler can't compile it yet") — a clean reject-don't-miscompile
;   rust: artifact did NOT build — error[E0308]: mismatched types (in the generated test DRIVER, not the lib)
;
; The emitted LIBRARY is VALID (compiles standalone): `pub fn main(s: String) -> i64 { (s.clone()).len() as
; i64 }`. So the fault is the rust-target DRIVER's STRING-ARGUMENT marshalling — the harness that calls `main`
; with the corpus arg `"abc"` passes it at a mismatched type (an E0308: almost certainly `&str`/`&String` vs
; the `String` the param wants, or a missing `.to_string()`/`.into()`), producing invalid Rust.
;
; ISOLATED (recompute-before-crying-bug, one axis at a time):
;   - String param on a HELPER (main takes Int64, calls the helper) → BUILDS + runs on BOTH backends. So a
;     String parameter per se is fine; the fault is a String at the EXPORTED-ENTRY / (call …) boundary.
;   - Int64/Bool/Float entry args → fine on both (every existing corpus `(call …)` uses these).
;   - The emitted library `fn main(s: String)` is valid standalone (rustc-clean); the E0308 is in the driver.
;   - No corpus case ANYWHERE calls an exported fn with a String ARG — every String-input case builds the
;     string INSIDE the program and passes only Int64/Bool/Float across `(call …)`. So this surface is wholly
;     untested, and it is broken on rust while wasm declines.
;   - VERIFIED CURRENT: no commit between my worktree base and trunk touched the rust backend / entry glue,
;     so this reproduces on current trunk (not a stale-base artifact).
;
; SUGGESTED FIX (v-rust-backend / the gate rust-driver String-arg marshalling): the driver must pass a String
; entry argument as an owned `String` (e.g. `"abc".to_string()` / `String::from("abc")`), matching the emitted
; `fn main(s: String)` signature — it currently passes a mismatched type → E0308. (Alternatively, if a String
; entry parameter is intentionally unsupported on rust, the rust path should DECLINE like wasm, not emit
; invalid Rust — the two backends must agree: both decline, or both accept.)
;
; The case below asserts the CORRECT result (byte-len "abc" = 3). It DECLINES on wasm and FAILS TO BUILD on
; rust today; the point is the two backends disagree — flip to a uniform outcome (both run → 3, or both
; decline) when fixed.

(case "adv rust-string-entry: an exported entry with a String parameter is called with a string argument"
  (doc "`(def (main (: s String)) (String.byte-len s))` exported and called `(call main \"abc\")` should
        yield the UTF-8 byte length 3. The emitted rust LIBRARY `fn main(s: String) -> i64` is valid, but
        the rust-target DRIVER that marshals the \"abc\" argument fails to build (E0308 mismatched types —
        a String entry argument passed at the wrong type). wasm cleanly DECLINES. A String parameter on a
        HELPER builds fine on both backends, so the fault is the exported-entry String-argument boundary
        specifically. Both backends must agree (both run → 3, or both decline); today they diverge.")
  (input (do (def (main (: s String)) (String.byte-len s)) (export main)))
  (call main (: "abc" String))
  (output (: 3 Int64)))

; SUBSUMED 2026-07-16 by the consolidated family issue: queue/adv-rust-nonscalar-entry-arg-driver-marshalling-family.sexp (rust driver cannot marshal ANY non-scalar entry arg — String/BigInt/Rational/Bytes — ONE root: driver writes raw Cadenza literal text into Rust source instead of the library construction form). Verified family gates wasm 1p/4todo vs rust 1p/4fail on trunk b29b7c89a. Track/promote via the FAMILY reproducer; this individual repro resolves under the same v-rust-backend fix. (Not renaming .RESOLVED yet — still reproduces; retire when the family fix lands.)

; ✅ RESOLVED 2026-07-16 (subsumed) — fixed under the family one-root fix 5a9a86c96 (rust_call_arg marshals ALL non-scalar entry args). Family reproducer gates 8/8 rust on trunk 6c1e89f65. This individual repro is covered by the family graded cases (09-functions/13-strings). CLOSED.
